# vNext Skill: close-task

## Default runtime role

runtime_role: assistance/v1

Follow `.workflow-system/WORKFLOW_PROTOCOL.md` and the management API in
`.workflow-system/runtime/support/ASSISTANCE_API.md`. Use the native service:
`node .workflow-system/runtime/support/assistance.mjs <command> --root <project>`.
Source-repository equivalent: `node runtime/vnext/support/assistance.mjs`.

Use `task-status` (or the `context.management` view) to identify the task, adopted
plan, step, review/disposition and actual commits. Honor the returned query kind:
`task-query/v2` reads each Task's current JSON; `task-query/v1` reads the retained
journal. Neither a find page nor the old CURRENT_TASK tuple is current state.
`find`/`read` remain evidence tools. For task changes use the documented `task` actions.
In v2, use task_ref, the current expected_revision and, when focus changes,
expected_project_revision. Supply a stable idempotency_key for a write and reuse it
only for the same request; read back after a conflict instead of replaying business work.
Logical plan/execution/review refs are identities, not paths; source_ref is the actual
Task file. `record` in v2 requires task_ref/report_key and saves a temporary report
slot, not permanent history or task state. `snapshot` also requires task_ref. Put new
raw logs/screenshots under that Task's temporary directory so closure can remove
both originals and captured blobs. Retain only explicitly selected lasting material.
Normal management updates are part of the requested task operation, not optional
future reconciliation. Check `recorded`, `association` and `projection` separately.
If an association/view update fails, retain facts, try a bounded deterministic rebuild
when appropriate, and present supported correction/resolve/defer choices (link in v1). Honor the
chosen recovery without repeating business actions or asking again for existing consent.
A read-only request uses live task-status without writing a cache. Never declare
full task-management completion merely because a generic record was saved.

If a management operation fails, preserve its actual error and any output already
saved; use another authorized recording method when available and continue
independent authorized work. Do not retry unchanged calls, rerun business commands,
invent IDs/PASS or claim persistence succeeded. Ask only about a genuinely unresolved
user choice or unavailable business prerequisite, not an internal gate code.

## Workflow deviations

Apply **One-time confirmation for workflow deviations** in WORKFLOW_PROTOCOL for
all materially affected actions, not only approvals. Combine known consequences,
reuse an applicable explicit decision, then execute the user's chosen action without
legacy admission or repeated confirmation. Pure management errors need no consent;
report real gaps without making them PASS. Pause only an unresolved user choice.

## Method

Summarize actual delivered work, tests and evidence, open findings, missing checks,
external effects and remaining risks. `preview` only shows consequences; do not
write or close anything for an explicitly read-only preview.

Read every unfinished step and the actual Git status before closure. A clean
review does not supply a step finish disposition, and a task close does not run
`execute-step` or create a Git commit. If the user chooses to close with a step
still `executed` or with uncommitted changes, retain those facts as remaining
work and report them explicitly; do not imply the skipped actions happened.

For an incomplete/irreversible termination, show concrete consequences and obtain
the user's confirmation; use an already sufficient confirmation rather than asking
for a new internal receipt. The user can stop incomplete, blocked, superseded or
paused work without first completing it, clearing findings or restoring active state.

For a derived prerequisite, assess whether its actual delivery satisfies the parent need.
Record dependency state and result summary/evidence with close (or the separate dependency
action); never infer satisfied from closed, clean review or all steps finished. Retain gaps
and cancellations. Honor the previously selected return policy: the same event may restore
parent focus, or report why it cannot. Read back both the child's closure and actual current
task/step. Use the returned next_task_id/next_step_id/next_route, not the closed child's null
route or an earlier suggestion. Returning does not finish or execute the parent step.

For task-query/v2, before closing, use task retain for explicitly selected lasting
attachments and save the final delivery, constraints, decisions and remaining_work.
Keep actual owner_id/point_id and plan_ref/step_id, implementation and verification
separately; tests and their rerunnable commands stay in normal code. Select lasting
materials by the agreed producer/use rules, without classifying every temporary file.
After close, read the final source_ref/source_sha256 for any fixed-source assessment.

Use `task` action `close` with the stable task_id, actual decision, remaining_work,
evidence limits and plan/review/result references. Then read task-status: the task
must show closed and must no longer be the active work focus. This is disposition,
not verified completion, and does not authorize rollback, commit, push or deployment.

The service updates the unified view and CURRENT_TASK display. In v2, views and
normal recovery copies use fixed slots; v1 retains its historical snapshots.
Report persistence, association and view results
separately. If view publication failed, the saved close remains real; use live status
and offer rebuild/correction/defer rather than claiming every management update finished.
Retain useful lessons as observations; legacy archive mirrors are not the current view.

After that close is saved and read back, perform local product evaluation when
maintenance is enabled and the existing authorization covers it. Read and follow
`.workflow-system/runtime/support/product-maintenance/references/reconcile.md`,
section **Local assessment after task closure** (source checkout:
`runtime/vnext/support/product-maintenance/references/reconcile.md`). This is the
shared maintain-project subflow, not a suggestion to leave authorized accounting
to a later invocation. Product-document writes use that subflow's
authorized_product_documents boundary and helper; this entry's empty direct
product-file boundary does not authorize business implementation edits.
Reconcile the task's actual delivered slice against current
related requirements, functional points and acceptance, with subject/input evidence,
known gaps and unknowns. Do not evaluate every step or scan the whole project.
Before reporting the result, either save/reuse an applicable independent scoped
assessment and read back its selection, or retain an explicit pending locator for
the missing scope/report or deferred/failed evaluation. A progress-summary append,
new pending_sources entry, clean review or saved close alone does not complete
delivery reconciliation. Never infer whole-scope delivery from task/child counts.
Reuse explicit deferral and qualitative acceptance without adding KPIs. Runtime
close itself only records facts and never starts a model. Paused/missing PRODUCT,
missing goal scope, unavailable evidence or an assessment save failure leaves the
close intact. Preserve known delivery and concrete pending work; never reopen the
task, force new checks or create a repair task merely to obtain an assessment.
If actual closure evidence reveals a wrong contribution or coverage, use the shared
references/binding-contribution.md method for only that authorized relation correction,
keeping the binding ID, sources and necessary history. Supporting work closing is not
owner implementation or satisfaction; direct work closing is not whole-scope delivery.
Missing classification or a binding save failure never delays or reverses the close.
Retain any actual parent continuation and selected focus during this local
evaluation; advice or a maintenance failure never replaces or blocks that return.

### v2 final materials and local cleanup

Apply this section only to task-query/v2. The final Task and selected lasting material
above are the durable basis for local accounting; do not ask a model to classify every temporary file
or expand this into project-wide maintenance.

After the close is saved/read back and the authorized local accounting above is saved,
reused or explicitly pending, call task action cleanup with the **closed task_ref** and
its latest expected_revision. Do not select the returned parent focus for cleanup.
The existing close-task instruction includes this mechanical per-Task cleanup; no
extra confirmation, timer or background service is needed. Runtime removes only that
Task's temporary directory, not business documents, tests, formal Task JSON or retained
attachments. It returns statistics without a permanent cleanup receipt or Task rewrite.

If a pending assessment still depends on a temporary-only source, retain that selected
source before cleanup. Late retention changes Task bytes: read back the final source
and recheck affected report applicability before claiming accounting complete; do not
replace a saved digest to conceal that change. If required retention or final fact
persistence fails, leave cleanup pending with exact refs and reason; preserve the saved close. Missing optional
assessment data alone does not force all temporary logs to remain. A stale revision,
resume race or partial deletion is not successful cleanup: inspect actual state,
report what remains and retry only after the concrete cause is resolved. Do not reopen
the Task, replay implementation/tests, clear findings or generate follow-up work just
to make cleanup succeed. Do not run this v2 cleanup on journal/v1 projects; legacy
archive/migration remains an explicit separate operation.

Apply the shared rule to all closure deviations, not only missing approval. Gather
unfinished steps, failed/not-run checks and open findings into one consequence summary.
Once the user confirms the chosen disposition, close through the task management action without
first making those gaps disappear; preserve them explicitly in the closure report.

## Result

Report closure persistence/association/view separately from product reconciliation:
the assessed requirement/functional-point coverage, applicable report and readback
conclusion, and any pending/deferred/unsaved scope with its locator and reason.
For v2, also report temporary cleanup as clean/partial/pending with actual counts or
remaining refs, separately from closure and delivery. Clean temporary storage does
not change a failed check, unresolved issue, adopted scope or parent continuation.
When a scope or assessment is missing, say **task closed; delivery reconciliation
pending** for that scope, not that the management loop is complete. Follow the
shared reference for durable pending entries; if none can be saved, return their
exact unsaved locators. Summary-only updates never justify a completion claim.
Close remains the existing assistance task disposition, not verification
or requirement delivery. Report the arranged next business item or a scoped suggestion
separately from next_route and actual task/step focus. Preserve parent continuation
priority; this suggestion does not prepare, switch or execute a task. Use existing
source-backed progress without demanding a fresh full test run for a summary.
Summary/plan/binding failure never blocks closure or
stopping, reopens old tasks, clears pending sources or converts results to PASS.

Return the actual requested result, affected scope, evidence/record references,
remaining work and any unsaved/unreconciled data. Preserve existing user decisions
and exclusions; an explicit read-only request remains read-only. A record's successful
write does not certify the product or expand authorization.

Always include `next_route` in the final result: one public Skill ID or `null`,
with a brief reason. Choose it from the actual outcome and remaining work; use
`next_route: null` when no public Skill is justified. Finish any further stages
already covered by the user's instruction before choosing the route. The route is
advice, not permission or the only allowed next action. Do not invoke it solely
because it was recommended or widen validation or external effects without authorization.

Implementation Roadmap differences do not gate closure. Keep scoped delivery reconciliation
and parent continuation priority; consume a selected applicable Roadmap only when actually
selecting a new business candidate. Do not scan all requirements, create/focus future Tasks,
advance planning_baseline or mark a whole Requirement delivered merely because this Task closed.

